A Woodpecker workflow publishes ONE commit status for all of its steps, so
`ci/woodpecker/cron/full-suite: failure` names no step, and one
chronically-red step makes every sibling's verdict unreadable for as long
as it stays red -- INV-bozid's MASKING half, accepted on 2026-08-30 with the
tripwire "if full-suite starts sitting red, unmask it".

It sat red on the third day, and this is the unmask. The pipeline object
behind a status's target_url carries every step's own state, and the log
fetcher was already reading it to pick the failed step; `cron-status` and
`status` now render it, one line per step (OK / FAIL (exit N) / ERR / SKIP /
KILL), per matrix leg for nightly. `error` and `skipped` are marked apart
from `success` because INV-bobor's third delivery failure was a pipeline
dying inside a gate reading as the gate passing. When the steps cannot be
read -- no Woodpecker credentials in .env, a refused fetch, a workflow index
the pipeline lacks -- the output says so and names why, rather than showing
nothing.

IT CAUGHT A MASKED SECURITY-GATE REGRESSION ON ITS FIRST LIVE RUN. The
